WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.780
- You see the hat?

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:05.550
I am Mrs. Nesbitt! (laughing)

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:07.494
- Snap out of it, Buzz!

00:00:07.494 --> 00:00:09.541
- Are you still trying
to digest all the content

00:00:09.541 --> 00:00:11.830
Disney announced at their Investor Day?

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:14.450
We did an entire episode on
their upcoming Star Wars shows

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.820
and still got blindsided
by the "Book of Boba Fett,"

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:17.950
so we feel your pain.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.170
After running through the
Marvel and Star Wars news,

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:21.800
we're still hanging in there to break down

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.550
the rest of Disney's upcoming slate

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.020
right here on The Ketchup.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.340
Fans were given their first clue

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.010
into what the "beyond" in
"to infinity and beyond"

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.780
might look like with the
Pixar prequel "Lightyear."

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:34.090
Tentatively scheduled for June 2022,

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:35.860
"Lightyear" will focus on the origins

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.640
of Tim Allen's Buzz
Lightyear action figures,

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:39.750
specifically the real-life space explorer,

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.870
voiced by Chris Evans, that
the "Toy Story" character

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:42.810
was modeled after.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.840
Though we didn't see any original footage

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.640
from the Angus MacLane-directed project,

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.250
promotional material hints at a mix

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:50.270
of the familiar and brand new Buzz.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.526
We'll be seeing the origins
of the heroic space ranger

00:00:52.526 --> 00:00:54.470
as he works to protect the galaxy,

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:56.510
but should expect our hero's personality,

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:58.610
just like his voice, to
be slightly different

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.530
than the one we've come
to know during the course

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:01.720
of the "Toy Story" films,

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:03.892
which shouldn't be a problem
considering fans equally love

00:01:03.892 --> 00:01:06.150
every entry in this franchise.

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:06.983
- Stranger.

00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:08.054
- From the outside.

00:01:08.054 --> 00:01:10.050
- [All Aliens] Ooh!

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:12.340
- But the expanded fun
doesn't stop at "Lightyear"

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.700
because Disney also announced seven series

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.260
that we'll be able to stream on Disney+,

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:17.950
four of which will expand the stories

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:19.760
of characters we already know and love.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:21.097
Like, remember that big marshmallow puff

00:01:21.097 --> 00:01:23.720
of a medical robot from "Big Hero 6?"

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:25.730
Well now, free to perform
his actual functions

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:27.080
as a nurse bot,

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:28.963
audiences can look forward
to following Baymax

00:01:28.963 --> 00:01:31.700
in his new self-titled
series as he explores

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:34.500
San Fransokyo finding new
friends and patients to help

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.490
sometime in early 2022.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:38.430
Helmed by the movie's director Don Hall,

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:41.440
"Baymax" is the second spinoff
of the popular franchise,

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:44.169
following 2017's "Big Hero 6" TV series,

00:01:44.169 --> 00:01:46.900
which ran for three seasons on Disney XD.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:48.660
But who cares about the superhero kids?

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.650
Give the lovable robot his own show.

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:53.537
- I will scan you now. Scan complete.

00:01:53.537 --> 00:01:55.010
- Meanwhile, get ready

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:57.760
for some meta programming
from the "Zootopia" universe,

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.351
which explores fan-favorite characters

00:01:59.351 --> 00:02:00.710
by making them the stars

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:02.730
of their own fictional reality shows.

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:04.930
Catch series like "So
You Think You Can Prance"

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:08.850
and "Life at Sloth Speed"
in 2022's "Zootopia+,"

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.620
which you can find on Disney+.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:11.680
See what they did there?

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:12.513
- Bingo!

00:02:12.513 --> 00:02:14.141
- Oh, pretty sneaky, slick!

00:02:14.141 --> 00:02:16.530
- Additionally, two Disney princesses

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:18.500
will also be getting
their own original series

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:20.320
that we'll be able to stream on Disney+.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.416
Picking up where "The Princess
and the Frog" left off,

00:02:22.416 --> 00:02:25.341
2022's "Tiana" follows Disney Animation's

00:02:25.341 --> 00:02:26.224
first black heroine

00:02:26.224 --> 00:02:28.350
as she adjusts life as royalty

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:29.960
in New Orleans's French Quarter.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:32.040
The following year brings us "Moana,"

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.810
which focuses on the lore
surrounding the Pacific Islands

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:37.419
that gave us the beloved
Maui from the original film.

00:02:37.419 --> 00:02:40.208
And I imagine this is Disney+
 to audiences right now:

00:02:40.208 --> 00:02:43.976
♪ What can I say except,
"You're welcome" ♪

00:02:43.976 --> 00:02:46.140
- Do you love Disney,
but just hate animation?

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.860
First of all, seek help, maybe?

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:49.460
But also Disney has you guys covered

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:50.547
in this department as well. Don't worry.

00:02:50.547 --> 00:02:52.915
First up is a new "Sister Act" sequel.

00:02:52.915 --> 00:02:55.080
Rumors have been circulating for years

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.970
about a follow-up to 1992's
nun-centric blockbuster

00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:59.600
and its sequel, "Back in the Habit."

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:02.140
But now, for the first
time, Disney is confirming

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.170
not only the green light, but the return

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:06.530
of star Whoopi Goldberg
as Delores van Cartier,

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:07.880
a singer on the run from the mob

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:09.770
who goes into hiding at a convent.

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:11.510
Although we don't yet have a release date,

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:13.980
Tyler Perry is confirmed
to produce for Disney+

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:16.665
the latest installment of a
now 20-year-old franchise.

00:03:16.665 --> 00:03:18.063
And I think it's safe to say that

00:03:18.063 --> 00:03:20.001
♪ I will follow him ♪

00:03:20.001 --> 00:03:23.440
(choir singing)

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:25.248
And finally, "Disenchanted" will see

00:03:25.248 --> 00:03:26.870
Amy Adams back as Giselle

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:30.070
in the long-awaited sequel
to 2007's "Enchanted."

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:31.770
So far, there are few other details

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.442
regarding the release
date or returning cast,

00:03:33.442 --> 00:03:36.090
but the follow-up to the
postmodern fairy tale

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:39.040
about a soon-to-be princess
cast out of her cartoon kingdom

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:41.383
of Andalasia and banished
to real-life Manhattan

00:03:41.383 --> 00:03:44.760
was originally slated for a 2011 release.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:46.420
So right now, fans are just happy to hear

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.020
that this film is happening at all.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:49.870
Signaling potential further delays,

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:52.690
"Disenchanted" director Adam
Shankman's "Hocus Pocus" sequel

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:55.460
was also revealed to be in
production during Investor Day,

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.650
meaning we may have to wait
just a little bit longer

00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:59.970
to find out what "happily ever
after" actually looks like

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:00.803
for Giselle and her friends.

00:04:00.803 --> 00:04:02.073
- I'm angry. I'm angry!

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:05.730
- All right, it is time to
throw it over to you, now.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:06.580
- What are your thoughts

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.830
on all these upcoming Disney shows?

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:10.270
Let us know in the comments section.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:12.109
And of course, if you want
more movie and streaming news,

00:04:12.109 --> 00:04:14.008
head on over to RottenTomatoes.com.

00:04:14.008 --> 00:04:15.770
And don't forget to check out

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:17.500
our brand new "Rotten Tomatoes is Wrong

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:19.120
(a podcast from Rotten Tomatoes),"

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:20.830
because Fresh or Rotten
is just the beginning

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:21.663
of the conversation,

00:04:21.663 --> 00:04:23.990
and new episodes drop every Thursday.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:24.828
As always, thanks for watching

00:04:24.828 --> 00:04:26.510
another episode of the Ketchup.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:27.890
My name is Naz Perez signing out

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:31.500
with my famous catchphrase:
"To infinity and beyond."

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:32.333
Bye!

